From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: lpass-wsa-macro: add the RX1 path control
 default

The WSA macro's register defaults have an entry for
CDC_WSA_RX0_RX_PATH_CTL but none for CDC_WSA_RX1_RX_PATH_CTL, although
it is a read/write register used by the WSA_RX1_CLK widget and the
"WSA_RX1 Digital Mute" control.

With the flat cache a read of it returned a zero-initialised cache
entry. With the maple cache it misses the cache, and while the macro is
runtime suspended and its regmap is cache-only the read fails with
-EBUSY. DAPM then takes the error code for the register value when the
card binds, and reading or writing the mute control fails until the
first playback has woken the macro.

Add the default, 0x04, the reset value of the matching RX0 register.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c
index 3c63043207a..5de54643c0c 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c
@@ -670,6 +670,7 @@ static const struct reg_default wsa_defaults[] = {
 	{ CDC_WSA_RX0_RX_PATH_MIX_SEC0, 0x08},
 	{ CDC_WSA_RX0_RX_PATH_MIX_SEC1, 0x00},
 	{ CDC_WSA_RX0_RX_PATH_DSMDEM_CTL, 0x00},
+	{ CDC_WSA_RX1_RX_PATH_CTL, 0x04},
 	{ CDC_WSA_RX1_RX_PATH_CFG0, 0x00},
 	{ CDC_WSA_RX1_RX_PATH_CFG1, 0x64},
 	{ CDC_WSA_RX1_RX_PATH_CFG2, 0x8F},
